; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Ulam Spiral
; CATEGORY: Number Theory
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     primes, spiral, sieve, dot, patterns
; SUMMARY:  Winds the counting numbers into a square spiral and puts a dot on every prime, revealing mysterious diagonal lines.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   In 1963 the mathematician Stanislaw Ulam was doodling during a
;   boring talk. He wrote 1 in the middle of the page, then 2, 3, 4...
;   winding outward in a square spiral, and circled the primes. To his
;   surprise the primes clustered along diagonal lines. Nobody can fully
;   explain why, even today. This program redraws his doodle with
;   more than 14000 numbers.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change :SIDE to make the spiral bigger or smaller, and
;   :GAP to change the space between dots.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a square spiral: walk 1, turn, 1, turn, 2, turn, 2, turn, 3...
;   * a sieve stored in an array, so each prime test is just ITEM
;   * DOT to mark a spot without drawing a line
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Start the spiral at 41 instead of 1 (add 40 to each number before
;     testing it). Euler's formula n*n + n + 41 makes a famous long
;     diagonal appear.
;   * Mark the even numbers instead of the primes. What do you see?
; ============================================================

; Make an array where item n is "true when n is prime.
to make.sieve :limit
  localmake "s (array :limit 1)
  for [i 1 :limit] [setitem :i :s "true]
  setitem 1 :s "false
  for [p 2 sqrt :limit] [
    if item :p :s [
      for (list "m :p * :p :limit :p) [setitem :m :s "false]
    ]
  ]
  output :s
end

; Each arm of the spiral is one straight walk. After every two arms the
; arms get one step longer; that is what makes the square grow.
to spiral :total
  localmake "n 1
  localmake "arm 1
  penup home setheading 90
  mark :n
  while [:n < :total] [
    repeat 2 [
      repeat :arm [
        if :n < :total [
          forward :gap
          make "n :n + 1
          mark :n
        ]
      ]
      left 90
    ]
    make "arm :arm + 1
  ]
end

; Primes get a dot. The color slowly shifts from orange near the
; center to blue at the edge, so you can see how far out you are.
to mark :n
  if not item :n :primes [stop]
  localmake "t :n / :total
  setpencolor (list 240 - 200 * :t 120 60 + 180 * :t)
  dot pos
end

make "side 121          ; an odd number, so 1 sits exactly in the middle
make "gap 4.2
make "total :side * :side
make "primes make.sieve :total

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [15 15 30]
setpensize 3
spiral :total
setpencolor "red setpensize 7 dot [0 0]
penup setxy -390 276 setpencolor "white setlabelheight 18
label (sentence [Ulam spiral of the first] :total [numbers])
